<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Galich</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Galich is a shallow lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kostroma">Kostroma</a> Oblast in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, covering about 75 square kilometres, with the town of Galich on its south-eastern shore. Its basin was settled by the Finnic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merya">Merya</a> before Slavic colonisation in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Archaeologists have found prehistoric remains, including the Galich hoard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> metalwork, near the lake.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-galich.jpg" alt="Lake Galich" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Florstein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_Balchug_hill_in_Galich_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
